  "title": "Erdős Problem #851",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $\\epsilon>0$. Is there some $r\\ll_\\epsilon 1$ such that the density of integers of the form $2^k+n$, where $k\\geq 0$ and $n$ has at most $r$ prime divisors, is at least $1-\\epsilon$?",
